SettingsCenter.GuiBackend.Description=Default graphical renderer. Automatic uses startup detection. Command-line choices override this value; unknown external renderer IDs are preserved.
SettingsCenter.GuiBackend.Label=Graphical renderer
SettingsCenter.GuiFont.Description=Choose a font for supported graphical frontends. A custom font can be entered manually.
SettingsCenter.GuiFont.Label=Graphical font
SettingsCenter.GuiFontSize.Description=Set graphical font size. This does not change the font of an external terminal emulator.
SettingsCenter.GuiFontSize.Label=Font size
SettingsCenter.GuiUseSystemMonospace.Description=Use the platform monospace font on supported Windows and macOS graphical frontends instead of the custom font.
SettingsCenter.GuiUseSystemMonospace.Label=Use system monospace font
SettingsCenter.HelpLanguage.Description=Choose the built-in help language independently of the interface language.
SettingsCenter.HelpLanguage.Label=Help language
SettingsCenter.HistoryDirsPrefixLen.Description=Width of the command-history directory prefix while date-and-time display is active. Minimum four characters.
SettingsCenter.HistoryDirsPrefixLen.Label=Command directory column width
SettingsCenter.HistoryShowTimes.0.Description=Choose the timestamp presentation independently for this history.
SettingsCenter.HistoryShowTimes.0.Label=Command history timestamps
SettingsCenter.HistoryShowTimes.1.Description=Choose the timestamp presentation independently for this history.
SettingsCenter.HistoryShowTimes.1.Label=Folder history timestamps
SettingsCenter.HistoryShowTimes.2.Description=Choose the timestamp presentation independently for this history.
SettingsCenter.HistoryShowTimes.2.Label=Viewer/editor history timestamps
SettingsCenter.InfoPanelBytes.Description=Display raw bytes instead of human-readable sizes in information and quick-view panels.
SettingsCenter.InfoPanelBytes.Label=Show sizes in bytes
SettingsCenter.InfoPanelCPUGPU.Description=Include locally collected CPU and GPU sections when the information provider does not supply authoritative information.
SettingsCenter.InfoPanelCPUGPU.Label=Show CPU and GPU information
SettingsCenter.KeepTerminalCursor.Description=Leave cursor-style management to the terminal instead of letting f4 change it.
SettingsCenter.KeepTerminalCursor.Label=Preserve terminal cursor style
SettingsCenter.Language.Description=Choose the language of the interface. Applying reloads resources and rebuilds Settings Center captions.
SettingsCenter.Language.Label=Interface language
SettingsCenter.MacKeyboard.Description=Use Mac-style editing chords in editors and dialog fields. Auto enables them on macOS; panels retain Far navigation. Command translation requires backend support.
SettingsCenter.MacKeyboard.Label=Mac keyboard mode
SettingsCenter.MacroRecordFormat.Description=Save recorded key macros in the legacy key_macros.ini format or as Lua scripts under Macros/scripts.
SettingsCenter.MacroRecordFormat.Label=Record macros as
SettingsCenter.NavigationMode.Description=Classic types into the command line. Vim adds j/k and double dd/cc/mm actions. Search-first separates filename-search and command focus.
SettingsCenter.NavigationMode.Label=Panel navigation
SettingsCenter.Next=Next match
SettingsCenter.PanelScrollbarMode.Description=Hide the scrollbar, show a minimal one, or show the full scrollbar with arrows.
SettingsCenter.PanelScrollbarMode.Label=Panel scrollbar
SettingsCenter.PathHintFullPath.Description=Display complete paths rather than only the final filename or folder component.
SettingsCenter.PathHintFullPath.Label=Show full suggestion paths
SettingsCenter.PathHintMaxVisible.Description=Maximum number of visible suggestion rows. Minimum 1.
SettingsCenter.PathHintMaxVisible.Label=Maximum visible suggestions
SettingsCenter.PathHintPerCategory.Description=Apply the visible-row limit separately to active-panel, passive-panel and history suggestions.
SettingsCenter.PathHintPerCategory.Label=Separate suggestion limits
SettingsCenter.PathHintSource.Description=Resolve suggestions from the active panel, passive panel, or both. Both searches active first.
SettingsCenter.PathHintSource.Label=Suggestion source
SettingsCenter.PathHintTimeout.Description=Maximum time allowed for a filesystem directory read behind suggestions. This is not a delay before suggestions appear. Minimum 1 second.
SettingsCenter.PathHintTimeout.Label=Directory read timeout (seconds)
SettingsCenter.Previous=Previous match
SettingsCenter.ProxyHost.Description=Hostname or address of the configured HTTP or SOCKS5 proxy.
SettingsCenter.ProxyHost.Label=Proxy host
SettingsCenter.ProxyMode.Description=Use system/environment proxy settings, direct connections, or an HTTP/SOCKS5 proxy for downloads and network providers unless overridden per connection.
SettingsCenter.ProxyMode.Label=Proxy mode
SettingsCenter.ProxyPass.Description=Password used to authenticate to the configured proxy. Its value is excluded from search.
SettingsCenter.ProxyPass.Label=Proxy password
SettingsCenter.ProxyPort.Description=Port of the configured HTTP or SOCKS5 proxy.
SettingsCenter.ProxyPort.Label=Proxy port
SettingsCenter.ProxyUser.Description=Username used to authenticate to the configured proxy.
SettingsCenter.ProxyUser.Label=Proxy username
SettingsCenter.RestoreWorkspaceTabs.Description=Recreate saved workspaces at startup instead of restoring only the initial workspace.
SettingsCenter.RestoreWorkspaceTabs.Label=Restore workspace tabs
SettingsCenter.SavePanelPaths.Description=Save panel folders and focused files. Turning this off omits these values from subsequently saved workspace sessions.
SettingsCenter.SavePanelPaths.Label=Save and restore panel paths
SettingsCenter.Search=Search:
SettingsCenter.SearchCommandStayFocused.Description=In Search-first mode, keep command entry focused after executing a command rather than returning to the panel.
SettingsCenter.SearchCommandStayFocused.Label=Keep command input focused
SettingsCenter.SearchExactOnHit.Description=The old hotkey table used this to narrow exact search hits. Settings Center uses dim-only search and does not consume this preference. Its saved value is retained.
SettingsCenter.SearchExactOnHit.Label=Legacy exact-hit preference
SettingsCenter.Select=Select a setting to read what it does.
SettingsCenter.SeparateFileExtensions.Description=Align the final extension separately in the name column. Excludes folders, extensionless names and leading dots alone.
SettingsCenter.SeparateFileExtensions.Label=Separate filename extensions
SettingsCenter.ShowDirPrefix.Description=Prefix folder names with a slash, unless a highlight rule already supplies one.
SettingsCenter.ShowDirPrefix.Label=Prefix folder names
SettingsCenter.ShowHiddenFiles.Description=Include hidden files and folders in the listing. The parent-directory entry remains visible.
SettingsCenter.ShowHiddenFiles.Label=Show hidden files
SettingsCenter.ShowHighlightMarks.Description=Show markers from matching file-highlight rules. Also affects path suggestions; symlinks retain their fallback arrow.
SettingsCenter.ShowHighlightMarks.Label=Show highlight marks
SettingsCenter.ShowPanelFileInfo.Description=Reserve a bottom row for the focused name, size and modification time. Short panels suppress this row.
SettingsCenter.ShowPanelFileInfo.Label=Focused-file status row
SettingsCenter.StartupMode.Description=Choose how plain f4 launches. Explicit --gui or --tty arguments override this default for that launch.
SettingsCenter.StartupMode.Label=Startup mode
SettingsCenter.SyncPanelLoad.Description=Replace the listing only when all directory results are ready and bypass cached previews. Off permits incremental results. It does not block all UI work.
SettingsCenter.SyncPanelLoad.Label=Wait for complete directory listing
SettingsCenter.TTYBackend.Description=Default terminal renderer. Command-line renderer choices override this preference.
SettingsCenter.TTYBackend.Label=Terminal renderer
SettingsCenter.TerminalCtrlNWorkspace.Description=Reserve Ctrl+N while terminal input has focus to create a workspace. Off sends the chord to the terminal program.
SettingsCenter.TerminalCtrlNWorkspace.Label=Ctrl+N creates workspace
SettingsCenter.Title=Settings
SettingsCenter.Capture=Capture
SettingsCenter.MatchCount=%d matching settings, collections and commands
SettingsCenter.UpdateChannel.Description=Check stable releases or nightly builds.
SettingsCenter.UpdateChannel.Label=Update channel
SettingsCenter.UpdateInterval.Description=Check never, every start, after at least 24 hours, or after at least seven days. Checks run at startup, not on a continuous timer.
SettingsCenter.UpdateInterval.Label=Check for updates at startup
SettingsCenter.UseExternalEditor.Description=Route ordinary Edit commands to an external editor. Remote files are temporarily downloaded and changes can be uploaded afterward.
SettingsCenter.UseExternalEditor.Label=Use external editor
SettingsCenter.UseLocalLanguageFiles.Description=Allow local language files to override bundled interface and help translations.
SettingsCenter.UseLocalLanguageFiles.Label=Use local translations
SettingsCenter.UseTrash.Description=Send ordinary Delete operations to trash where supported. Explicit permanent-delete commands still delete permanently.
SettingsCenter.UseTrash.Label=Use trash or recycle bin
SettingsCenter.ViewerAutodetectCodePage.Description=Detect encoding when opening the viewer or a quick-view preview.
SettingsCenter.ViewerAutodetectCodePage.Label=Detect viewer encoding
SettingsCenter.ViewerDefaultCodePage.Description=Fallback viewer and quick-view encoding when detection is disabled or inconclusive.
SettingsCenter.ViewerDefaultCodePage.Label=Default viewer encoding
SettingsCenter.WheelEditorDown.Description=Number of editor rows per downward wheel notch. Zero follows the system setting.
SettingsCenter.WheelEditorDown.Label=Editor wheel down
SettingsCenter.WheelEditorUp.Description=Number of editor rows per upward wheel notch. Zero follows the system setting.
SettingsCenter.WheelEditorUp.Label=Editor wheel up
SettingsCenter.WheelMenuDown.Description=Number of menu rows per downward wheel notch. Zero follows the system setting.
SettingsCenter.WheelMenuDown.Label=Menu wheel down
SettingsCenter.WheelMenuUp.Description=Number of menu rows per upward wheel notch. Zero follows the system setting.
SettingsCenter.WheelMenuUp.Label=Menu wheel up
SettingsCenter.WheelPanelDown.Description=Number of panel rows per downward wheel notch. Zero follows the system setting.
SettingsCenter.WheelPanelDown.Label=Panel wheel down
SettingsCenter.WheelPanelUp.Description=Number of panel rows per upward wheel notch. Zero follows the system setting.
SettingsCenter.WheelPanelUp.Label=Panel wheel up
SettingsCenter.WheelTableDown.Description=Number of table rows per downward wheel notch. Zero follows the system setting.
SettingsCenter.WheelTableDown.Label=Table wheel down
SettingsCenter.WheelTableUp.Description=Number of table rows per upward wheel notch. Zero follows the system setting.
SettingsCenter.WheelTableUp.Label=Table wheel up
SettingsCenter.WheelViewerDown.Description=Number of viewer rows per downward wheel notch. Zero follows the system setting.
SettingsCenter.WheelViewerDown.Label=Viewer wheel down
SettingsCenter.WheelViewerUp.Description=Number of viewer rows per upward wheel notch. Zero follows the system setting.
SettingsCenter.WheelViewerUp.Label=Viewer wheel up
SettingsCenter.WorkspaceTabMode.Description=Show tabs always, only with multiple workspaces, while Ctrl is held, or never.
SettingsCenter.WorkspaceTabMode.Label=Show workspace tabs
SettingsCenter.WorkspaceTabNumbering.Description=Keep numbers permanently, keep them during this session, or renumber to match the current tab order.
SettingsCenter.WorkspaceTabNumbering.Label=Workspace numbering
SettingsCenter.WorkspaceTabsOverlay.Description=Draw workspace tabs over the content instead of reserving a layout row.
SettingsCenter.WorkspaceTabsOverlay.Label=Overlay workspace tabs
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltEdit.Description=Command dispatched for this slot, using the existing user-menu substitution machinery.
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltEdit.Label=AltEdit command
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltEditEnabled.Description=Enable this association command slot. An empty command is skipped.
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltEditEnabled.Label=Enable AltEdit
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltExec.Description=Command dispatched for this slot, using the existing user-menu substitution machinery.
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltExec.Label=AltExec command
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltExecEnabled.Description=Enable this association command slot. An empty command is skipped.
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltExecEnabled.Label=Enable AltExec
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltView.Description=Command dispatched for this slot, using the existing user-menu substitution machinery.
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltView.Label=AltView command
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltViewEnabled.Description=Enable this association command slot. An empty command is skipped.
SettingsCenter.assoc.AltViewEnabled.Label=Enable AltView
SettingsCenter.assoc.Description.Description=Name shown when several associations match.
SettingsCenter.assoc.Description.Label=Description
SettingsCenter.assoc.Edit.Description=Command dispatched for this slot, using the existing user-menu substitution machinery.
SettingsCenter.assoc.Edit.Label=Edit command
SettingsCenter.assoc.EditEnabled.Description=Enable this association command slot. An empty command is skipped.
SettingsCenter.assoc.EditEnabled.Label=Enable Edit
SettingsCenter.assoc.Execute.Description=Command dispatched for this slot, using the existing user-menu substitution machinery.
SettingsCenter.assoc.Execute.Label=Execute command
SettingsCenter.assoc.ExecuteEnabled.Description=Enable this association command slot. An empty command is skipped.
SettingsCenter.assoc.ExecuteEnabled.Label=Enable Execute
SettingsCenter.assoc.Mask.Description=Select filenames for which this association is considered.
SettingsCenter.assoc.Mask.Label=Filename mask
SettingsCenter.assoc.View.Description=Command dispatched for this slot, using the existing user-menu substitution machinery.
SettingsCenter.assoc.View.Label=View command
SettingsCenter.assoc.ViewEnabled.Description=Enable this association command slot. An empty command is skipped.
SettingsCenter.assoc.ViewEnabled.Label=Enable View
SettingsCenter.binding.Action.Description=Stable action identifier to invoke. Existing action IDs and plugin actions remain supported.
SettingsCenter.binding.Action.Label=Action
SettingsCenter.binding.Area.Description=Input context in which this binding is considered. Common is the fallback for other areas.
SettingsCenter.binding.Area.Label=Area
SettingsCenter.binding.Condition.Description=Optional registered condition checked when dispatching the action. Empty means unconditional.
SettingsCenter.binding.Condition.Label=Condition
SettingsCenter.binding.Key.Description=Far-style chord spelling, such as CtrlShiftF. An empty chord leaves the action unassigned.
SettingsCenter.binding.Key.Label=Chord
SettingsCenter.bookmark.Path.Description=Directory path or expandable path expression for this numbered slot.
SettingsCenter.bookmark.Path.Label=Folder path
SettingsCenter.grant.Keep.Description=Clear to revoke this remembered answer on Apply. The next protected request asks again. This control cannot create grants.
SettingsCenter.grant.Keep.Label=Remember permission
SettingsCenter.link.Hotkey.Description=Far-style shortcut spelling, such as Q or CtrlF5.
SettingsCenter.link.Hotkey.Label=Shortcut
SettingsCenter.link.Name.Description=Display name in the drive chooser.
SettingsCenter.link.Name.Label=Link name
SettingsCenter.link.Path.Description=Directory or provider path opened by the link.
SettingsCenter.link.Path.Label=Link path
SettingsCenter.menu.binary.Commands.Description=Multiline shell commands using existing user-menu substitutions.
SettingsCenter.menu.binary.Commands.Label=Commands
SettingsCenter.menu.binary.HotKey.Description=Menu activation key. Use -- for a separator.
SettingsCenter.menu.binary.HotKey.Label=Activation key
SettingsCenter.menu.binary.Label.Description=Visible command or submenu name.
SettingsCenter.menu.binary.Label.Label=Label
SettingsCenter.menu.binary.Parent.Description=Empty places the item at the root. Otherwise select the ID of a submenu entry.
SettingsCenter.menu.binary.Parent.Label=Parent entry ID
SettingsCenter.menu.binary.Submenu.Description=Group child entries under this item instead of executing commands.
SettingsCenter.menu.binary.Submenu.Label=Is a submenu
SettingsCenter.menu.local.Commands.Description=Multiline shell commands using existing user-menu substitutions.
SettingsCenter.menu.local.Commands.Label=Commands
SettingsCenter.menu.local.HotKey.Description=Menu activation key. Use -- for a separator.
SettingsCenter.menu.local.HotKey.Label=Activation key
SettingsCenter.menu.local.Label.Description=Visible command or submenu name.
SettingsCenter.menu.local.Label.Label=Label
SettingsCenter.menu.local.Parent.Description=Empty places the item at the root. Otherwise select the ID of a submenu entry.
SettingsCenter.menu.local.Parent.Label=Parent entry ID
SettingsCenter.menu.local.Submenu.Description=Group child entries under this item instead of executing commands.
SettingsCenter.menu.local.Submenu.Label=Is a submenu
SettingsCenter.menu.main.Commands.Description=Multiline shell commands using existing user-menu substitutions.
