SettingsCenter.Text.37f7bcf678fc5e867821f3b252ba6743a1a9a6baccfe147968c4e0f6addf5618=Used only when GEMINI_API_KEY, GOOGLE_API_KEY and OPENAI_API_KEY are all empty, in that precedence order. Effective source: %s (if a key is available). The key is stored in the local vtvibe.ini file.
SettingsCenter.Text.8c67fcfa12a69b6c3e8edfa20bc751404ebc8a282b951884f8027a6bf25c8bd5=Choose a renderer using startup detection. Avoids pinning a backend that may be unavailable on another machine; the selected backend can change with the environment. Applies on the next graphical launch.
SettingsCenter.Text.cf64399345c0b3f6ab1273b664c01f8104c461f4f04bfddd1ce61e344b0793be=Native Windows graphical window using GDI drawing. Does not require the GoGPU or Ebitengine graphics stack; useful when those backends have driver problems. Windows only, and drawing performance differs from GPU backends. This is a separate window, not the Windows console renderer.
SettingsCenter.Text.3b4f2fa1d5894f413e8422470600127f79bb43c8b5d59beaa766e9868cf13cff=Graphical window rendered through GoGPU. Uses a GPU drawing pipeline for text and graphics. Requires compatible graphics drivers and FFI support in this build; graphics initialization can fail where the native or terminal renderer works. No universal speed advantage is guaranteed.
SettingsCenter.Text.4fbd9fb4e3334f60dabd8eb7bb936243f619bc01076db8da52e16d8c1237dc38=Graphical window using Ebitengine's rendering and input loop. Provides an alternative graphics stack when another GUI backend behaves poorly. Requires graphics-driver and FFI support; window, input and performance behavior can differ from the native backend.
SettingsCenter.Text.f1ea43776711d0be7ca69375a69bd1d55a048440db4f1bd617d9f81b11beae29=Connect directly to an X11 display server. Useful in an X11 desktop or an environment with an accessible X server; does not require the GoGPU graphics stack. Requires an X server and display access. On a Wayland desktop it needs an X11 compatibility service such as XWayland.
SettingsCenter.Text.88946e8ef7ef507847998947af5a31a112ada6b16a130062657c71ec0b13ab79=Connect to a Wayland compositor instead of an X server. Fits a native Wayland session without requiring XWayland for this window. Requires a compatible Wayland session and FFI support; it cannot serve as the native Windows GUI backend.
SettingsCenter.Text.c419cc2ce2c809dfaff777e1957695235cfc023b177e6d0cf19570a082ddc7b1=Follow startup environment detection. May choose a graphical window where supported; native Windows and Wine retain terminal startup by default. Explicit command-line mode takes precedence.
SettingsCenter.Text.189f229f6888d316ccaf4c25aeff43dd75cc3f242ae2e665e3eea8d38c5c22d6=Start inside a terminal even when a graphical desktop is available. Uses the terminal renderer preference; the terminal host controls its own font and window.
SettingsCenter.Text.7f787d6e08593f446072b15ba43ba313ded48a7564bee57a9e0591e89848c704=Start in a separate graphical window, including on Windows. Uses the graphical renderer preference and requires that backend to be available.
SettingsCenter.Text.7ade2382857f15ca4f461208e0d4317c0b8857c295883105a95cb96d9af10351=Detect the appropriate terminal output method at startup. Convenient across different hosts; choose an explicit renderer if detection gives unsuitable colors or behavior.
SettingsCenter.Text.e4abde1a8b1d885f175b432e7f6b9e0910710c44f48d67e430b00d645217c4d4=Write ANSI/VT escape sequences to the terminal. Suitable for modern terminal emulators, including Windows Terminal; available colors and input features depend on the host.
SettingsCenter.Text.0e6e8310e9c15589dbea9042766f48364b67e2c972f414b042ff725cace1100e=Use the Windows console API rather than ANSI output. Intended for Windows console compatibility. Color representation and behavior differ from ANSI output; prefer ANSI when using a modern terminal's extended capabilities.
SettingsCenter.Text.4904906fd93d020dd632d01423fca2eddc471017c321f8b2495987bb2a0c99f0=Keep the workspace tab bar visible even with one workspace. Easier to discover, but occupies space unless tabs overlay the content.
SettingsCenter.Text.7473c44aebe16ea5474a63886728f0c04dc93a430ae691c191001670d8f51079=Show the tab bar only when multiple workspaces exist. Saves space while working in a single workspace.
SettingsCenter.Text.ca50079f0323e0adbc1f34160d7ff75dc3f7f31d2bb1d9f96c37c7507f156f38=Show the tab bar while Ctrl is held. Keeps the display compact but hides workspace labels the rest of the time.
SettingsCenter.Text.404d6e5275484acbf6e67c3fa62250a818f75fa720cacf1544ee1d135fb1abdb=Hide the workspace tab bar. Workspaces remain accessible through their switching commands and shortcuts.
SettingsCenter.Text.267a8f06e79b4991266788419a54e672c924ebffe98f365d8289d6e60665d701=Keep workspace numbers stable and restore them with saved workspaces. Reordering tabs does not renumber them.
SettingsCenter.Text.fd181e75fd8c2ba9d608eec5b3d519dc3d812bf89525b86166b09ef0a1ae6b90=Keep workspace numbers stable during the current run without preserving that numbering across restarts.
SettingsCenter.Text.164d67e1b10864892de76e3615b2d570eab008a73a2a57d6a9171932d0f02b38=Number workspaces by their current order. Moving or removing a tab can change the numbers used for switching.
SettingsCenter.Text.4da29bb0aa4cb2c4a7dff80ba4ff54894f5e0b5189e5b54b5e8e5be70a70df28=Do not draw a panel scrollbar. Navigation still works with the keyboard and mouse wheel.
SettingsCenter.Text.66a4e985058e3bdc83a92d369bfccc8721f03d754bea8fd987c0772e92231a72=Show a compact scrollbar without the full arrow decoration. Provides position feedback with less visual detail.
SettingsCenter.Text.f8f0f6ba56ac57eec6d8987f997f55b3baf9dce871dd8b0f710d090d3376fbe1=Show the complete panel scrollbar, including arrows. Makes scrolling controls more explicit.
SettingsCenter.Text.ec31315d2f42b1f62aa1f7a71b0c315d4e571d9a985c73a3f52a90415f63a80a=Typing goes to the command line while ordinary panel navigation keys move the file cursor. Familiar Far-style behavior.
SettingsCenter.Text.c82bdc0d8cdfe8665b991d8b24d61c4606b707cc435fac24f059c99a2dfb3025=Enable Vim-style panel navigation, including j/k and double dd/cc/mm actions. Letter keys can invoke panel actions instead of entering command text.
SettingsCenter.Text.9c5f91305b38385da92bf29720b890ee405d2ea7f1b3eeb20ab0ba84979033c2=Separate filename-search focus from command-entry focus. Convenient for finding files by typing; entering shell commands requires command focus.
SettingsCenter.Text.12bf79940bf30e65ce783cd361f0db49ad5fe93c02ed8889812be270e27cbf0c=Read path suggestions from the active panel's filesystem and location.
SettingsCenter.Text.f7ffc36cab02f0704c07a35f89b53c140921cd462b292853f3faeddca6432f38=Read path suggestions from the passive panel's filesystem and location.
SettingsCenter.Text.fda7f436332c9e889f4644aa416d40052acea29d7ea147c5e11cf2851f21d808=Read suggestions from both panels, active first. Offers more candidates but may require reading two locations.
SettingsCenter.Text.ceb6f5e5ae839ea194fd68513084360ad017ebd7d65174d275eb17e8c009365e=Put a new operation in the operation queue. Useful for controlling simultaneous work instead of starting every operation independently.
SettingsCenter.Text.a6ef58834232cdbe89e5369dd7c2a4f4fcbc8cca2076c659c81051bc632da18c=Start in the background so panel work can continue. Several operations may compete for the same disk or connection.
SettingsCenter.Text.7a04b4c336a0257c2a182159717d509fd8fd462649cfc49b7f243096dc211d99=Start with the operation progress in the foreground. Keeps progress and prompts in view while the operation runs.
SettingsCenter.Text.5ef7ae398f62bcd16f482c3c72a2edd10299b291affb49aad75bd50dfdd51bf8=Show only the current item's name. Compact, but identical names in different folders are harder to distinguish.
SettingsCenter.Text.3f9bc56c8a125bfcefff1e4600f0ed2bf8c25271e0c2689c13b40cce8d754da9=Show the current item's full path. Identifies its folder, but long paths need more display space.
SettingsCenter.Text.595b6669b5929aa16e42a12a786608d91d49af1df073befcf38320cd138a3191=Show source and destination paths. Useful for checking where files go, at the cost of more progress text.
SettingsCenter.Text.cd62c61825b655a74cb1a21981e43f5b39e96c8f71511c31fb472458c2caa57b=When content normalization is enabled, ignore differences in line endings while retaining other whitespace differences.
SettingsCenter.Text.9ddf0a5e36864537cf7da56dffa93dd53d393b804e6b8680c220c798a31b8977=When content normalization is enabled, ignore all whitespace differences. May treat files with meaningfully different spacing as equal.
SettingsCenter.Text.d7d82dcd163ddfd6761d9ccec285d6d40092285ab62cc2682144551cedfb731c=Pressing Tab inserts a tab character. Its displayed width follows tab stops; the file keeps a literal tab.
SettingsCenter.Text.de3b5f078657a5faa92f6885fba217d6b882167286781c046d9da66dfad19d8c=Pressing Tab inserts spaces up to the next tab stop. Existing tab characters are not converted.
SettingsCenter.Text.3b40a95375fec4e7aaed9abdec891cd8ef73768f73205e63b1b587f825f160e3=Legacy All value: currently inserts spaces exactly like Spaces. It does not convert existing tabs; the legacy value is preserved until you change it.
SettingsCenter.Text.9fa88ac079ddaccdf43535f4645b1a8e8fd82f6ee2e15c7979a32df213ee257d=Draw no cursor guide lines, even if the crosshair switch is enabled.
SettingsCenter.Text.48326e9174c796a335e120a0a8295ed319281bc2b54bff67b4b5590056bdb312=Draw a vertical guide through the cursor column when crosshair display is enabled.
SettingsCenter.Text.a8ec1037702b9a641e718631a96fdd65635aeef94b338f857a4ff4486463259f=Draw a horizontal guide through the cursor row when crosshair display is enabled.
SettingsCenter.Text.8337107d5ea675cce0702c010cd863f476c74a537942328bc2a04fcb2c444078=Draw both cursor guides when crosshair display is enabled. Makes row and column alignment explicit, but adds more lines to the text area.
SettingsCenter.Text.4a8bb929ad96374dc45759fedbfb0d8677e8a33051ea220032c2af71ee183f24=Use the bundled Chroma syntax engine. Does not require Colorer's external schemas; its language rules and colors differ from Colorer.
SettingsCenter.Text.b54d5f151044cd7ccaa1e6dff537e38abed8dbba0c5c126d0cf4aadb86615698=Use Colorer syntax schemas and styles. Supports its configurable scheme data, but needs installed schemas and can fall back if they are unavailable.
SettingsCenter.Text.66913610bfd33055181edb7d0e4fa367507f0a49a3861c1d3d55a82f90408cff=Disable syntax highlighting in newly opened editors. Avoids syntax coloring work and shows text using the ordinary editor palette.
SettingsCenter.Text.f75db9fdf1854fbe9bce5bf34233636b3b3726189f6e0e1d0266f9e4d93cb10f=Use the built-in default Colorer scheme rather than a named installed HRD scheme.
SettingsCenter.Text.7763567cecd6d64bd32c6ca495d30ed5f61244e3c37f9b0ae0096d4651dadaf7=Enable Mac-style editing chords on macOS and ordinary editing chords elsewhere. Backend support is still needed for Command-key translation.
SettingsCenter.Text.60f4ce4d7f6bfc3167ed215bc7411978ddbb765a79f2c39ed7af8ce4acb504d0=Force Mac-style editing chords in supported editors and dialog fields. Panel navigation stays Far-style; Command translation depends on the backend.
SettingsCenter.Text.4e3f8b832d02f866212c38194f541012bd3e92adbb9e501b6fb554df370866da=Use ordinary editing chords even on macOS. Does not change the panel navigation model.
SettingsCenter.Text.d8197e7e440015fae45ef3c2935ebec614e4dbe8da753aa099dc01ef946a65a5=Use f4's embedded terminal. Keeps terminal presentation inside the workspace rather than relying on a host-terminal overlay.
SettingsCenter.Text.13cd86950cf8b97b6efc64b9ef950f5815efbcf2664a52edecbb0386cd84f5e0=Use the host terminal with f4's overlay where supported. Resembles Far-style interaction; unsupported hosts can fall back to another presentation.
SettingsCenter.Text.5659de5a317f3af8f5c78b6b488d60d5325cc150bd94f48f5d560ca8e0eea598=Use the host terminal without f4's overlay where supported. Resembles MC-style presentation; availability depends on terminal capabilities.
SettingsCenter.Text.dc0d43342b58b7e0d19730e47a8486750b04cc49d4260d43eca4e5f2d386a175=Show both date and time for entries in this history.
SettingsCenter.Text.06f93796619d85324377516ee30d5b5e99f1ad814ea7139f0ac7ebf3ef3aa57e=Show only the date for entries in this history, reducing timestamp detail.
SettingsCenter.Text.4d952df1bcb3e288744edff4c06738c83022d95ca10720fb2a0becd3461fee2e=Hide timestamps in this history. Entries remain stored; only their presentation changes.
SettingsCenter.Text.16b757447181f2b6c6edc75a2da394d2edb52efc31f1a73ef9584e3791ec6dc5=Save newly recorded key macros in key_macros.ini. Keeps the legacy recording format.
SettingsCenter.Text.5660cc985e64cc9ee5360a411f7f7c003161887e37963b9c909d907a686f4409=Save newly recorded macros as Lua scripts under Macros/scripts. Produces script files that can be edited afterward.
SettingsCenter.Text.6af705eb7c7ab707fd6f5d93bcf4423630b2ac69dd32d59273207c032c2049e4=Use system or environment proxy configuration. Convenient for managed environments; the actual route can change with those external settings.
SettingsCenter.Text.c750a8c5370b0e272e9e5938638bff566848580620414a9e3c2062ac1a14815f=Connect directly, without the configured proxy. A destination that requires a proxy may be unreachable.
SettingsCenter.Text.c458b7ad813a1e843abda9f07650838566494d9065d6c65482b66fe63b4bd88b=Route supported requests through the HTTP proxy at the configured host and port. Optional proxy credentials apply to this route.
SettingsCenter.Text.5a7cce7727d22810cae9ee5eb62fd6a9951f7da82303d3ac9d712d9d557a3bd3=Route supported connections through the SOCKS5 proxy at the configured host and port. Requires a reachable SOCKS5 server.
SettingsCenter.Text.742a77953b4e956caae6ca176d14c2740af8749d9c11a9f6cbf252c5b18d4fb0=Look for stable releases. Favors published release versions over the latest development builds.
SettingsCenter.Text.dd7d9930ddb9ebb3e4b79a76b190aa056ce45a1d07f3a88e64be181e6a5e6287=Look for nightly builds. Gets newer development changes earlier, with a greater chance of regressions than stable releases.
SettingsCenter.Text.e9e1153e5e517b2059d8348c8878e5962ea250eb409bad8b65dea44be27cba7d=Do not check automatically at startup. The explicit Check Now command remains available.
SettingsCenter.Text.78764d2480c467926d8b0f6bf6bc7a5f568f12090e1efda788023593dc39feb7=Check whenever f4 starts. Does not create a continuously running update scheduler.
SettingsCenter.Text.b03e22249c17a9dd3de24e9a6f49c5de56936eb218609876dd8e3198a3531253=At startup, check if at least 24 hours have elapsed since the previous check. Keeping f4 open does not trigger another check by itself.
SettingsCenter.Text.1d9436fcba56bba1e1d91ba5ab11372dd309065cca34168443b2fc33048af8f8=At startup, check if at least seven days have elapsed since the previous check. This is not a weekly background timer.
SettingsCenter.Text.333f90986f14fc18cc1ed3e0e32edd86cc5b2429d7b7a13d0f5c77daf1630481=An environment profile contains variable assignments. When enabled, it participates in ordered environment reconciliation after Apply.
SettingsCenter.Text.47de5e06464039f2a843f3a54608f20c7df35754b816e428a78ba84d97a9a13e=An organizational separator in the profile list. Does not apply variable assignments to the process or shells.
SettingsCenter.Text.66e800694d83c9913fde577869ae89cc7a02fe4a818f4a1921c736f780e76602=Show original and target names together in the rename editor. Easier to compare each proposed name with its source.
SettingsCenter.Text.92eefe907117fce9319777a413d1b10471aa16ab19c7ace17af2d973567d6d73=Show only target names in the rename editor. More compact and easier to transform as a plain list, but original names are not alongside them.
SettingsCenter.Text.1709408481c941eeefc137ad99f5b87a304c23efb98e342fb61fa39b86bc9300=Use FTP. Suitable for FTP servers, but ordinary FTP does not encrypt credentials or file data. Do not assume SSH protection from this protocol.
SettingsCenter.Text.5fec1c881c8b7a7af215ba1304f3ef43d9366329cd7486a7b7230a0a5c5e87b6=Use the SSH file-transfer subsystem. Encrypts the connection and requires an SSH server with SFTP support.
SettingsCenter.Text.9737a4e29e93fec21b7428e6f331fb349366495ebb2e56ce630477d8c72fda9f=Transfer files through commands in a remote SSH shell. Useful when SFTP is unavailable, but requires a compatible remote shell and utilities.
SettingsCenter.Text.190f56be105b58b653841a13b0563abbed4919db56664f37be786345802cd86e=Use f4's applied global proxy settings for this connection. Later global proxy changes also affect this connection.
SettingsCenter.Text.049973a0cef5262d79df0c53005197457f6ec9ba13f3e53778fc9680fa218992=Store credentials in the operating system's keyring. Integrates with the current user's secret store; this is not the portable-profile storage option.
SettingsCenter.Text.6df76246fd91e9ffd64fe86927c89482c88d754f81a6ece9db1ac186ac6a1085=Store credentials in CloudFox's encrypted vault. Used for portable profiles; access follows the vault's unlocking workflow.
SettingsCenter.Text.da14b9f189731c1a36f3ce083b06d02693cb5a6c689cf14bfd1dd687dd06d1b7=Retain existing secrets and merge nonempty replacements entered in this draft. Blank secret fields do not clear saved credentials.
SettingsCenter.Text.81b1fc7e28b0692670c04dccda2fb653224e007971c0671a8ff485e3254357e6=Replace the complete saved credential bundle with the entered values. Credentials omitted from the replacement are not retained.
SettingsCenter.Text.31a662fdb48d389cc5d9762002010baae9fee52a5325f57540bdc4bd6988ef8d=Explicitly remove all stored credentials for this connection on Apply. Reauthentication may be needed before connecting again.
SettingsCenter.Text.a44abcd8c5c3ac48081f5d49020bd6b50043baec87440f582f437848e5806771=Let the AWS SDK resolve credentials through its default chain. Useful for configured environments or machine roles; the effective identity can come from outside this saved connection.
SettingsCenter.Text.0c6d834d161ea81eadeb156caaf88d0a08a584dfe727a5a9bfc958ad25b51cca=Use the named AWS profile. Convenient for shared AWS configuration; requires that profile to exist on this machine.
SettingsCenter.Text.008c1ff68fb97906e7825f03d391c2d2bb332fda3e434a4dc7306f7537314f37=Use the explicitly supplied access key, secret key and optional session token. Predictable identity, but expiring credentials must be updated.
SettingsCenter.Text.f96aae9203820a1e2b66cfb39340a4d9651d5e562cb080b891c12b27823515b2=Send S3 requests without signing them with credentials. Works only for resources that allow anonymous access.
SettingsCenter.Text.692dc5054fc9425a2fcfe9fe5a861b8968ae7d6b9012b235cad5715166b3c4f0=Authenticate with a username and password using HTTP Basic. Requires protected transport according to the provider's connection policy.
SettingsCenter.Text.577e28f45a5b12ecc2fe4ea0940bb7ee9ad10e9ff0ab2e7d80ae726b50a24d7e=Use HTTP Digest challenge-response authentication. The server must support it; unencrypted transport requires the separate permission setting.
SettingsCenter.Text.2da370fe1bd734d8be879c0af32adee32a2c4d659b1a8bd536a189cf1a15d966=Authenticate with the supplied Bearer token instead of a username/password exchange. Access depends on the token's permissions and lifetime.
SettingsCenter.Text.a2d419499f292a30e04544f5785aaebc51ccf4e777d251f9cb2bfe818a781064=Do not send authentication credentials. Use only for WebDAV resources that permit anonymous access.
SettingsCenter.Matches=Matches: %d
SettingsCenter.ClearSearch=Clear search
SettingsCenter.Category.hotkeys=Hotkey Configurator
SettingsCenter.Text.8802174070f1412801a7f0343b685b2031869bce18833d79e48e7a712ab59883=Prefer exact shortcut search matches
SettingsCenter.Text.c0010901537ebb36a8ae08ecdecf613679d66a4f8dcad5856094bc3752fcbf1d=In the Hotkey Configurator table, narrow the search to exact matches when available. This does not affect the Settings Center sidebar search.
SettingsCenter.Text.ac559d59a8e0f357fa1fc6da653bff0feb6a2f4aaf219e4ac9adf0b68e1c2128=next open
SettingsCenter.Text.a3a43e00b84aa7aca574eafb93a4feaf77b4287a615be9a7434ae99552df13e3=The Hotkey Configurator lists configurable, native and plugin shortcuts. Use Assign or Unbind; native shortcuts are read-only. Changes are saved with Apply or OK.
